{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'git diff e6522ceb..b825498e'","aggregated_output":"git: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-uxjOGLYE' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-07 02:16:12.579 xcodebuild[48529:113257201]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-07 02:16:12.916 xcodebuild[48529:113257198] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-LlxvNLAo' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-07 02:16:14.018 xcodebuild[48541:113257339]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-07 02:16:14.207 xcodebuild[48541:113257328] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc b/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\nindex c50abeab..484518ab 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\n@@ -80,24 +80,13 @@\n    on every `:application` node, at every depth the row grammar knows.\n    Literal payloads are data, never syntax, and are not walked. Marking\n    is idempotent and preserves node metadata and every other key, so\n-   canonical rows, roots, and executable outcomes are unchanged.\"\n+   canonical rows, roots, and executable outcomes are unchanged.\n+\n+   The walk itself is `yang.core.uast/annotate-call-sites`, shared with\n+   the other frontends' module trees; this frontend owns the contract's\n+   constants and its validation over canonical rows.\"\n   [node]\n-  (let [tag (:type node)\n-        slots (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar tag)]\n-    (when-not slots\n-      (throw (ex-info \"Unknown AST node type\" {:type tag, :node node})))\n-    (let [walked (reduce (fn [n [field kind]]\n-                           (case kind\n-                             :node (update n field annotate-call-sites)\n-                             :nodes (update n field\n-                                            (fn [children]\n-                                              (mapv annotate-call-sites\n-                                                    children)))\n-                             n))\n-                         node\n-                         slots)]\n-      (cond-> walked\n-        (= :application tag) (assoc call-site-key call-site-version)))))\n+  (u/annotate-call-sites node))\n \n \n (defn eligible-application-sites\n@@ -105,11 +94,23 @@\n    `origin`: one `[origin root-address path]` per `:application`\n    occurrence, derived from the occurrence relation and the row tags.\"\n   [tree origin]\n-  (let [{:keys [root rows]} tree]\n-    (into #{}\n-          (comp (filter (fn [[_ _ id]] (= :application (nth (get rows id) 1))))\n-                (map (fn [[_ path _]] [origin root path])))\n-          (vm/occurrences tree))))\n+  (into #{}\n+        (map (fn [[root path]] [origin root path]))\n+        (vm/application-occurrences tree)))\n+\n+\n+(defn call-site-metadata\n+  \"The C1 frontend-metadata rows of canonical `tree` (`{:root :rows}`)\n+   under `origin`: one `[origin root-address path :yang/call-site 1]`\n+   per eligible application occurrence, in printed-row order. This is\n+   the finalizer for trees that exist only as canonical rows — the\n+   expander's final tree, a published module's tree — where no map AST\n+   remains for `annotate-call-sites` to walk.\"\n+  [tree origin]\n+  (vec (sort-by pr-str\n+                (map (fn [[root path]]\n+                       [origin root path call-site-key call-site-version])\n+                     (vm/application-occurrences tree)))))\n \n \n (defn marked-application-sites\n@@ -124,24 +125,59 @@\n         (distinct frontend-metadata)))\n \n \n+(defn- marker-row?\n+  \"True when frontend-metadata `row` claims the C1 key: a sequential row\n+   whose fourth coordinate is `call-site-key`. A claiming row of any\n+   other arity is malformed, never a row to filter away silently.\"\n+  [row]\n+  (and (sequential? row)\n+       (<= 4 (count row))\n+       (= call-site-key (nth row 3))))\n+\n+\n (defn validate-call-site-coverage!\n   \"Validate a complete-coverage C1 claim: the marker set of\n    `frontend-metadata` for canonical `tree` under `origin` must equal\n    the eligible application set. Returns true when the claim holds.\n+\n+   A row that claims the C1 key but is not a five-coordinate\n+   `[origin root-address path key value]` row is malformed and is\n+   rejected, never silently filtered. The delivery mode is `opts`:\n+\n+   - default (transport): the relation arrived over a medium, where an\n+     at-least-once delivery may repeat a row; duplicate identical\n+     deliveries dedupe to the same fact;\n+   - `{:declared? true}`: the relation is a declared canonical table —\n+     the side table a producer published as the tree's table — where a\n+     duplicate entry is a second, conflicting claim to one fact and is\n+     rejected.\n+\n    Conflicting values at one site, an unsupported marker version, a\n    marker naming no occurrence, a marker on a non-application\n    occurrence, and missing or extra markers each throw, naming the\n    failed `:rule`.\"\n-  [tree frontend-metadata origin]\n-  (let [{:keys [root rows]} tree\n-        tag-at (into {}\n-                     (map (fn [[r path id]] [[r path] (nth (get rows id) 1)]))\n-                     (vm/occurrences tree))\n-        eligible (eligible-application-sites tree origin)\n-        rows (filter (fn [row]\n-                       (and (= 5 (count row)) (= call-site-key (nth row 3))))\n-                     (distinct frontend-metadata))\n-        by-site (group-by (fn [[o r path _ _]] [o r path]) rows)]\n+  ([tree frontend-metadata origin]\n+   (validate-call-site-coverage! tree frontend-metadata origin {}))\n+  ([tree frontend-metadata origin {:keys [declared?]}]\n+   (doseq [row frontend-metadata]\n+     (when (and (marker-row? row) (not= 5 (count row)))\n+       (throw (ex-info \"Malformed call-site marker row\"\n+                       {:rule :yang/call-site-malformed, :row row}))))\n+   (when declared?\n+     (doseq [[row n] (frequencies (filter marker-row? frontend-metadata))]\n+       (when (< 1 n)\n+         (throw (ex-info \"Duplicate call-site marker in a declared table\"\n+                         {:rule :yang/call-site-duplicate-entry,\n+                          :site (vec (take 3 row)), :row row})))))\n+   (let [{:keys [root rows]} tree\n+         tag-at (into {}\n+                      (map (fn [[r path id]] [[r path] (nth (get rows id) 1)]))\n+                      (vm/occurrences tree))\n+         eligible (eligible-application-sites tree origin)\n+         rows (filter (fn [row]\n+                        (and (= 5 (count row)) (= call-site-key (nth row 3))))\n+                      (distinct frontend-metadata))\n+         by-site (group-by (fn [[o r path _ _]] [o r path]) rows)]\n     (doseq [[site srows] by-site]\n       (when (< 1 (count (distinct (map #(nth % 4) srows))))\n         (throw (ex-info \"Conflicting call-site marker values\"\n@@ -170,18 +206,21 @@\n                                                 (remove marked eligible))),\n                          :extra (vec (sort-by pr-str\n                                               (remove eligible marked)))}))))\n-    true))\n+    true)))\n \n \n (defn validate-ast-call-sites!\n   \"Validate the C1 claim of a produced map AST `ast` under `origin`:\n    project it and compare the eligible application set derived from its\n    canonical rows with the marker set of its frontend-metadata side\n-   table. Returns true when the sets are equal.\"\n+   table. The projected table is a declared canonical table, so it is\n+   validated strictly (`:declared? true`). Returns true when the sets\n+   are equal.\"\n   [ast origin]\n   (let [tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n         tables (vm/ast-side-tables ast tree origin)]\n-    (validate-call-site-coverage! tree (:frontend-metadata tables) origin)))\n+    (validate-call-site-coverage! tree (:frontend-metadata tables) origin\n+                                  {:declared? true})))\n \n \n (defn literal?\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc b/src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc\nindex 30efcd0a..f203b2ca 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc\n@@ -166,10 +166,13 @@\n \n \n (def module-uast\n-  \"The linked module tree built from the same `definitions`.\"\n+  \"The linked module tree built from the same `definitions`. C1\n+   finalized, like every published production tree: its\n+   `:yang/call-site` markers publish beside its manifest (see\n+   `yin.vm.linker.publish`).\"\n   (let [stripped (core/module-definitions \"yang.call\" :yang.call/uninit\n                                           [] definitions)]\n-    (core/module-tree stripped [])))\n+    (u/annotate-call-sites (core/module-tree stripped []))))\n \n \n (def module-exports\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc b/src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc\nindex f1414ddb..da597c68 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc\n@@ -18,7 +18,8 @@\n      (f a ...)         -> :application\n      any other value   -> :literal\"\n   (:require\n-    [yang.tails :as tails]))\n+    [yang.tails :as tails]\n+    [yin.vm :as vm]))\n \n \n (defn lit\n@@ -105,3 +106,46 @@\n   \"`yang.tails/mark-tails`: the lowering marks its tree with the same\n    function a rewriting stage recomputes the marks with.\"\n   tails/mark-tails)\n+\n+\n+;; =============================================================================\n+;; Call-site occurrence contract C1 (Addendum A, design §2)\n+;; =============================================================================\n+;;\n+;; Every final `:application` occurrence of a produced tree carries the\n+;; reserved frontend-metadata key `:yang/call-site` with version value `1`\n+;; as a plain node key. Projection (`yin.vm/ast-side-tables`) drops the key\n+;; from canonical rows and emits it into the frontend-metadata side table\n+;; as `[origin root-address path :yang/call-site 1]`, where the first\n+;; three coordinates are the site id. The key carries no callee identity,\n+;; source arity, or ambient classification. It is distinct from\n+;; `:yang/site`, the safepoint mark, which travels as node metadata.\n+;; Dedicated node kinds (`:dao.stream.apply/call`, stream and\n+;; continuation nodes) are not `:application` nodes and are never marked.\n+;; The walk lives here, beside the other shared tree transforms, so every\n+;; frontend's module trees finalize the same way; `yang.clojure` owns the\n+;; contract's validation over canonical rows.\n+\n+(defn annotate-call-sites\n+  \"The finished map AST `node` with `:yang/call-site 1` on every\n+   `:application` node, at every depth the row grammar knows. Literal\n+   payloads are data, never syntax, and are not walked. Marking is\n+   idempotent and preserves node metadata and every other key, so\n+   canonical rows, roots, and executable outcomes are unchanged.\"\n+  [node]\n+  (let [tag (:type node)\n+        slots (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar tag)]\n+    (when-not slots\n+      (throw (ex-info \"Unknown AST node type\" {:type tag, :node node})))\n+    (let [walked (reduce (fn [n [field kind]]\n+                           (case kind\n+                             :node (update n field annotate-call-sites)\n+                             :nodes (update n field\n+                                            (fn [children]\n+                                              (mapv annotate-call-sites\n+                                                    children)))\n+                             n))\n+                         node\n+                         slots)]\n+      (cond-> walked\n+        (= :application tag) (assoc :yang/call-site 1)))))\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc\nindex 41c2e59a..df87de90 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc\n@@ -38,6 +38,20 @@\n    :yang.frontend/support-profile :segment/legacy})\n \n \n+(defn clojure-manifest\n+  \"The Clojure frontend's manifest. Its coverage promise changed under\n+   the call-site occurrence contract C1 — every final `:application`\n+   occurrence carries `:yang/call-site` in the frontend-metadata side\n+   table, finalized over the post-expansion tree that executes and\n+   retained beside a published module's manifest — and that promise is\n+   a support claim, so the revision and the support profile name it;\n+   the shared legacy profiles no longer describe this frontend.\"\n+  []\n+  (assoc (manifest :yang/clojure :clojure)\n+         :yang.frontend/revision \"c1-1\"\n+         :yang.frontend/support-profile :yang.clojure/c1))\n+\n+\n (defn- clojure-lower\n   [forms]\n   (if (= 1 (count forms))\n@@ -77,7 +91,7 @@\n    returns.\"\n   []\n   (cond-> frontend/empty-catalog\n-    true (frontend/install (manifest :yang/clojure :clojure)\n+    true (frontend/install (clojure-manifest)\n                            {:input :forms,\n                             :parse identity,\n                             :lower clojure-lower})\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc\nindex b0d222ca..1bb7ca84 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc\n@@ -1609,6 +1609,20 @@\n                (into tuples (map (fn [[path id]] [root path id]) frontier)))))))\n \n \n+(defn application-occurrences\n+  \"The `[root path]` of every `:application` occurrence of the projected\n+   row set `tree`: the occurrence relation joined on the row tags, with\n+   no origin — a composition fixes the origin from its own side, as with\n+   `occurrences`. This is the eligible-site derivation of the call-site\n+   occurrence contract: one pair per place, so a shared application row\n+   at two places counts twice.\"\n+  [{:keys [rows] :as tree}]\n+  (into #{}\n+        (comp (filter (fn [[_ _ id]] (= :application (nth (get rows id) 1))))\n+              (map (fn [[root path _]] [root path])))\n+        (occurrences tree)))\n+\n+\n (def occurrence-rules\n   \"§4.5/§7.7: root-scoped occurrence rules, as portable data. A name is\n    bound at `[root path]` iff a `:lambda` occurrence of the same root sits\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc\nindex 1bda6def..18c49562 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc\n@@ -227,6 +227,67 @@\n                               {:rule :batch-member, :member member}))))\n \n \n+(def ^:private call-site-key\n+  \"The reserved frontend-metadata key of the call-site occurrence\n+   contract C1 (`yang.clojure`), enforced at this boundary but not\n+   owned by it.\"\n+  :yang/call-site)\n+\n+\n+(defn- marked-call-sites\n+  \"The `[path value]` of every node of map AST `ast` carrying the C1\n+   key, walked by the row grammar. Literal payloads are data, never\n+   syntax, and are not walked. Member ASTs are already projected by the\n+   time this runs, so every tag is a grammar tag.\"\n+  [ast]\n+  (letfn [(walk\n+            [node path]\n+            (into (if (contains? node call-site-key)\n+                    [[path (get node call-site-key)]]\n+                    [])\n+                  (mapcat (fn [[j [field kind]]]\n+                            (let [pos (+ j 2)\n+                                  value (get node field)]\n+                              (case kind\n+                               