{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"**REJECT for landing.** The fix resolves parts of the four findings, but the side tables still have custody and validation defects.\n\n1. **F1 remains incomplete.** The expander constructs C1 metadata over the final tail-marked, stand-in-lowered tree, but [macro/load](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1395) keeps only one `:frontend-metadata` value. The next successful expansion overwrites the previous tree’s table, while the executed tree remains on `program-out`. The new test checks one load, so it does not establish coverage retrieval across successive REPL evaluations. The expander also creates C1 metadata unconditionally, including for batches whose frontend made no C1 claim.\n\n2. **F2 remains incomplete for a transported publication.** [publish-module!](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:260) stores the table and a reverse record beside the manifest, but the manifest does not reference either. The module closure follows manifest references, so transferring the published module’s closure does not carry the table or record. The [retrieval test](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:311) uses the original store, where those otherwise unreachable objects still happen to exist. Also, [call-site-claim](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:127) checks paths but not marker values: a complete table containing version `2` is accepted and stored, while `published-call-site-table` looks only for a reconstructed version-`1` table and returns `nil`.\n\n3. **F3 and F4 are addressed for the requested cases.** The validator rejects malformed rows that claim the key and distinguishes duplicate transport deliveries from duplicates in a declared table. The Clojure catalog entry now has revision `c1-1` and support profile `:yang.clojure/c1`.\n\nThe mislabeled expansion-origin test was removed. The new post-expansion and publication tests cover the single-expansion and same-store cases described above, but do not close the residual defects. This was a static review of `e6522ceb..b825498e`; I did not rerun the supplied remote test results."}}
